a. conducts socialization regarding the prevention of Violence against women and children by optimizing the role of customary institutions, Education, culture, religion and community organizations;

b. builds networks and cooperation with law enforcement apparatus, government apparatus, universities and various non-governmental organizations that work and/or care for women and children victims of Violence;

c. provides public facilities that are comfortable and safe for women and children; and

d. establishes an Integrated Service Center for Women and Children Empowerment P2TP2A established by decree of the Mayor and provides a Secretariat for the Integrated Service Center for Women and Children Empowerment.

Article 42

(1) The City Government in efforts to protect and fulfill the rights of Children is responsible for:

a. establishing and implementing policies and programs/activities for the protection and fulfillment of the rights of Children;

b. respecting and guaranteeing the human rights of every Child without distinguishing ethnicity, religion, race, class, gender, ethnicity, culture and language, legal status of the Child, birth order of the Child, and physical and/or mental condition;

c. strengthening and developing institutions providing family quality improvement services in realizing the rights of Children;

d. guaranteeing the Protection, care, and welfare of Children with due regard to the rights and obligations of parents, guardians, or other persons legally responsible for the Child;

e. providing facilities and infrastructure in the implementation of the fulfillment of the rights of Children;

f. guaranteeing the right of Children to express opinions in accordance with the age and level of intelligence of the Child;

g. conducting supervision and guidance in the context of implementation; and

h. cooperating with private parties in the implementation of Child Protection.

(2) The responsibility of the City Government in efforts to Protect Children as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented by PD in accordance with their duties and functions.

Article 20

